@ [ECS_correspondence] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\ECS_Semantic_Fabric_Correspondence_2026-08-05.sop

& [ConceptualPlanes] keep semantic roles distinct
  + [governance_plane] owns TaskContract, principal, authority, policy, faculty cycle, Observer disposition, and signature references
  + [planning_plane] owns objectives, dependencies, alternatives, estimates, PlanRevision, schedule candidates, review gates, and residuals
  + [temporal_plane] owns TimeExpression, CalendarItem, recurrence, availability, commitment, wake, miss, cancellation, and completion revisions
  + [repository_plane] owns MaterialEvent, ContentObject, SemanticSnapshot, RepositoryGeneration, attribution, retention, and index projections
  + [transition_plane] owns ChangeCapsule, declared intent, diff surfaces, execution outcome, ReflectionReturn, invalidation, and after state
  + [lane_plane] owns prospective, execution, retrospective, join, lease, timeout, message, acknowledgment, release, and fault state
  + [compiler_plane] owns source and dependency generations, SemanticIR, target artifacts, correspondence, loss, proof, and invalidation
  + [learning_plane] owns forecast error, plan deviation, semantic surprise, LessonCandidate, review, and optional training-example candidate
  = must: connect planes through explicit identities and relations rather than field reuse or temporal proximity

& [IdentityRules] are stable and generation-aware
  + every durable subject has a UUID independent of filename, line, list position, timestamp, digest, or model narration
  + immutable generations additionally bind parent identity, predecessor identity set, semantic version where applicable, and content digest
  + revisions share a stable subject identity while each revision has its own revision UUID and predecessor revision
  + digests prove content equality only and do not replace identity, provenance, attribution, authority, or temporal occurrence
  + physical database keys or ECS handles are surrogates and cannot become canonical identity

& [RepositoryGeneration] is one admitted semantic frontier
  + [repository_uuid] is stable repository identity
  + [generation_uuid] is immutable generation identity
  + [predecessor_generation_set] is zero or more exact admitted predecessors
  + [repository_policy_ref] binds materiality, attribution, retention, sensitivity, compaction, and projection policies
  + [event_frontier] is the closed ordered set of admitted MaterialEvent identities
  + [snapshot_root_ref] binds the canonical SemanticSnapshot when materialized
  + [reference_index_generation] identifies replaceable derived indexes
  + [created_by_disposition] binds ObserverJoin admission evidence
  + [root_digest] commits canonical normalized generation content
  + [status] is candidate, admitted, superseded, revoked, quarantined, or archived

& [TaskContract] governs one work lineage
  + [task_uuid] is stable
  + [purpose] is explicit and source-linked
  + [principal_set] names eligible decision and effect principals
  + [input_and_target_refs] bind exact source, identity, file, artifact, or external-resource scopes
  + [preconditions] and [assumptions] are separately represented
  + [invariants] apply across every task transition
  + [authority_and_capability_request] is not a grant
  + [effect_boundary] declares possible effects and required brokers
  + [completion_contract] declares evidence, review, residual, and stop conditions
  + [privacy_and_retention_profile] binds task-specific information handling
  + [current_plan_revision_ref] selects one admitted plan without erasing prior plans

& [ObjectiveAndDependencyModel] supports Planner
  + [ObjectiveNode] has objective UUID, task UUID, statement, desired-state criteria, priority source, uncertainty, status, and proof route
  + [DependencyEdge] has edge UUID, predecessor objective or artifact, successor objective, dependency kind, condition, strength, source, and invalidation rule
  + [ConstraintNode] has constraint UUID, kind, scope, expression, source, severity, and disposition behavior
  + [AlternativePath] has alternative UUID, ordered or graph path, prerequisites, estimate range, effects, risks, review gates, fallback, and stop
  + [PlanRevision] has plan UUID, revision UUID, predecessor revision, task UUID, objective graph root, dependency graph root, temporal graph root, effect graph root, review graph root, selected alternative, assumptions, uncertainty, and state
  + one TaskContract has zero or more PlanRevision records and at most one current admitted revision
  + one PlanRevision owns one or more objectives and may own zero or more alternatives
  + cycles require an explicit iteration contract, termination condition, and budget

& [TimeExpression] preserves domains and uncertainty
  + [time_expression_uuid] is stable
  + [domain] is civil, instant, monotonic, logical, valid, transaction, or uncertain
  + [value] is point, interval, duration, set, partial date, or symbolic condition
  + [source_ref] is mandatory for asserted time
  + [zone] and [calendar_system] apply to civil time
  + [precision] and [uncertainty_interval] are explicit
  + [interpretation_policy_ref] governs ambiguous or nonexistent civil times
  + [conversion_evidence] binds conversion to another domain
  + [valid_from_and_to] describe subject applicability
  + [recorded_at] is transaction time and cannot substitute for valid time

& [CalendarItem] is stable across immutable revisions
  + [calendar_item_uuid] is stable subject identity
  + [revision_uuid] and [predecessor_revision_ref] form revision history
  + [kind] is task, block, appointment, deadline, reminder, wake, recurrence, or review
  + [task_contract_ref] is required for Cantor work items
  + [purpose] and [source_ref] are explicit
  + [owner_and_participant_refs] bind principals without implying their consent
  + [time_expression_refs] bind start, end, duration, deadline, or window as applicable
  + [recurrence_rule_ref] is optional, bounded, timezone-aware, and exception-capable
  + [dependency_and_review_refs] bind prerequisite and ChangeCapsule expectations
  + [authority_state] is proposed, eligible, granted, denied, revoked, or expired
  + [lifecycle_state] is proposed, tentative, accepted, declined, committed, triggered, active, completed, missed, cancelled, or superseded
  + [provider_sync_state] is local_only, pending, synchronized, divergent, failed, or revoked and remains separate from lifecycle
  + [sensitivity_and_disclosure] bind field-level privacy projection

& [RecurrenceRule] is finite under evaluation
  + [recurrence_uuid] is stable
  + [frequency_and_interval] are explicit
  + [zone_and_calendar] are explicit
  + [start_boundary] is required
  + [end_boundary_or_occurrence_limit] is required for bounded expansion windows
  + [inclusion_and_exception_sets] preserve overrides, skips, and moved occurrences
  + [materialization_horizon] prevents unbounded event generation
  + each occurrence has stable derived identity tied to rule revision and occurrence key
  + rule revision never rewrites already committed or observed occurrence history

& [MaterialEvent] is append-only and materially scoped
  + [event_uuid] is stable occurrence identity
  + [repository_generation_input] is exact predecessor generation
  + [task_contract_ref] and [attribution_ref] are mandatory when work-attributed
  + [event_kind] is observation, decision, semantic_transition, tool_request, tool_result, effect_request, effect_result, review, calendar, fault, admission, reentry, or compaction
  + [subject_ref_set] identifies affected semantic subjects
  + [content_object_ref_set] binds immutable payloads without requiring all sensitive content in the event row
  + [valid_time_ref] and [transaction_time_ref] remain separate
  + [materiality_decision] records rule, evidence, and disposition
  + [authority_and_effect_refs] bind claims without implying successful effect
  + [predecessor_event_set] forms causal or ordering edges where proved
  + [retention_class] and [sensitivity_class] are explicit
  + [event_digest] commits normalized event content

& [MaterialityPolicy] controls capture cadence
  + durable events include task opening, admitted plan, semantic transition, tool boundary, effect boundary, review barrier, calendar commitment or trigger, yield, fault, reentry, completion, and selected milestone
  + micro-events require declared liveness, diagnosis, audit, or measurement need
  + aggregation records the covered event class, interval, count, source, summary method, loss, and rehydration status
  + expiration records policy, authority, tombstone, and proof impact
  + materiality revisions apply prospectively and do not retroactively make omitted events observed
  + ordinary sequential capture never claims atomic external-world state

& [ContentObjectAndSnapshot] preserve immutable payload and state
  + ContentObject has object UUID, digest algorithm, digest, byte length, media type, encoding, provenance, sensitivity, retention, and storage locator set
  + locator changes do not change ContentObject identity when bytes and provenance remain exact
  + SemanticSnapshot has snapshot UUID, repository UUID, predecessor snapshot set, event frontier, canonical state root, projection manifest, content refs, and digest
  + snapshot branches are explicit and merges name all parents plus reconciliation evidence
  + compaction creates a new derived ContentObject or Snapshot with correspondence and loss records
  + deletion or redaction uses authorized tombstone and proof-impact records rather than history rewrite

& [ChangeCapsule] is the transition waist
  + [change_uuid] is stable across the transition attempt
  + [candidate_generation_uuid] distinguishes revisions or retries of one attempt
  + [task_contract_ref] and [plan_revision_ref] bind governing intent
  + [repository_generation_ref] and [before_snapshot_ref] pin admitted input
  + [declared_intent_ref] binds target set, expected transformations, allowed effects, completion proof, and unrelated-state exclusions
  + [prepared_candidate_ref] is optional before execution
  + [execution_request_and_outcome_refs] are distinct
  + [candidate_snapshot_ref] exists before admission and is not the after state
  + [physical_diff_ref], [source_diff_ref], [semantic_diff_ref], [build_diff_ref], [behavioral_diff_ref], [effect_diff_ref], [proof_diff_ref], and [calendar_diff_ref] remain separate
  + [justification_delta], [support_delta], [requirement_delta], and [compiler_impact_ref] are explicit
  + [reflection_return_ref] is required unless a signed omission or bounded-lag rule applies
  + [observer_join_ref] records reconciliation
  + [after_snapshot_ref] exists only after admission
  + [capsule_state] follows the legal lifecycle

& [DiffRecord] is evidence-bearing
  + [diff_uuid] is stable
  + [diff_kind] is physical, source, semantic, build, behavioral, effect, proof, or calendar
  + [before_subject_ref] and [candidate_subject_ref] are exact
  + [added], [changed], [removed], [preserved], and [unrelated] sets are separately identified
  + [derivation_method] and [independent_evidence_ref] declare how the diff was formed and checked
  + [confidence_or_completeness] remains explicit
  + [invalidation_output_set] lists dependent identities and reasons
  + [loss_and_unknown_set] cannot be coerced to no_change

& [LaneAndMessageModel] prevents shared-state races
  + [LaneCursor] has cursor UUID, lane kind, task UUID, input repository generation, plan revision, capsule generation, dependency set, authority request, state, lease, timeout, and last message
  + [LaneKind] is prospective, execution, retrospective, or observer_join
  + [LaneMessage] has message UUID, sender cursor, receiver cursor or join, subject version, payload refs, required acknowledgment, causal predecessors, created logical time, and expiry condition
  + [WorkPacket] is a bounded prospective or execution request with exact input generation and permitted outputs
  + [ReflectionReturn] has return UUID, retrospective cursor, exact capsule generation, disposition, evidence, objections, uncertainty, invalidation mask, residual, and signature or provider qualification
  + [ObserverJoin] has join UUID, expected lane returns, exact versions, received returns, stale checks, reconciliation record, disposition, successor proposal, and release set
  + lanes exchange immutable messages and never share mutable canonical state
  + one ObserverJoin admits at most one successor RepositoryGeneration for one capsule candidate

& [LaneLifecycle] is explicit
  + idle -> prepared -> running -> returned -> released
  + prepared may become blocked_on_authority, blocked_on_reflection, stale, invalidated, timed_out, cancelled, or failed
  + execution cannot run without separate authority and pinned predecessor
  + retrospective return cannot review a different capsule generation
  + join refuses stale or missing returns and records residual rather than deadlocking indefinitely
  + bounded lag records eligible transition class, maximum count or duration, consequence bound, rollback capacity, overdue behavior, and authority

& [CompilerWalkModel] binds SMTC generations
  + CompilerGeneration has compiler-generation UUID, source generation set, dependency lock, LanguageProfile, compiler identity, SemanticIR root, TargetProfile set, target artifact set, correspondence, loss, diagnostics, proof bundle, and state
  + forward stages are source_pinned, parsed, resolved, lowered, and projected
  + rear stages are source_diffed, semantic_diffed, impact_analyzed, correspondence_checked, and proof_checked
  + reconciled generation may become admitted, rejected, or invalidated
  + CompilerImpact records changed source or semantic identities and invalidated IR nodes, indexes, packages, schedules, workflows, model artifacts, tool schemas, and hardware artifacts
  + target generator output cannot be its only correspondence evidence
  + prior failed or superseded generations remain immutable

& [LearningModel] preserves review and provenance
  + ForecastError binds one preserved forecast, actual observations, comparison method, uncertainty, and affected future planning fields
  + PlanDeviation binds plan revision, actual sequence, deviation classes, reasons, effects, and review
  + SemanticSurprise binds newly exposed identity, meaning, dependency, or boundary with source and contradiction checks
  + LessonCandidate binds contributing capsules, proposal, eligible scope, counterexamples, confidence, review state, invalidation, and rollback
  + TrainingExampleCandidate binds lesson candidate, exact redacted source projection, consent and sensitivity policy, label provenance, evaluation split, and admission state
  + adoption creates a new separately reviewed SOP, policy, estimate profile, or corpus generation and never rewrites the old plan

& [OwnershipAndAuthority] are explicit
  + source authors own preserved source attribution but cannot self-sign derived authority
  + task principal owns commitment choices within eligible scope
  + Planner owns candidate projection, not truth or commitment
  + Calendar owns local versioned temporal representation, not provider synchronization authority
  + Scribe owns recording discipline, not truth
  + execution broker owns bounded effect mediation, not purpose revision
  + retrospective reviewer owns a qualified return, not final admission
  + Observer owns reconciliation disposition within signed policy, not external effect authority
  + retention or deletion authority is separately declared per content and jurisdiction profile

& [SensitivityModel] is field and relation aware
  + classes are public, project_internal, personal, confidential, secret, credential, regulated, and unknown_sensitive
  + calendar title, participant, location, routine, availability, and free-form notes may have different classes
  + source, diff, prompt, provider payload, tool result, trace, proof, and training example are classified independently
  + indexes and embeddings inherit or strengthen access restrictions because they may disclose source relationships
  + query relevance does not authorize disclosure
  + export projections state omitted or redacted fields and proof consequences

& [RetentionAndCompaction] are policy controlled
  + each event, content, snapshot, diff, trace, and lesson has retention class, minimum proof retention, maximum operational retention, archive rule, and deletion authority
  + transient micro-events may expire after aggregate proof when permitted
  + durable source, authority, effect, review, fault, admission, and signature evidence retain immutable lineage
  + compaction must be replay-equivalent within a declared observation boundary and preserve loss records
  + redaction creates explicit replacement or tombstone lineage
  + Git retention and semantic-repository retention are separate

& [VersionAndInvalidation] propagate exact change
  + source, contract, plan, calendar, repository policy, materiality policy, retention policy, profile, compiler, SemanticIR, target, provider, proof, and runtime versions are independent
  + invalidation is an edge with cause, source generation, affected subject, required rebuild or review, severity, and resolution
  + stale prepared work is rejected at CompareAndAppend
  + calendar wake revalidates assumptions, dependencies, authority, target identity, relevance, privacy, and effect scope
  + model or provider staleness cannot invalidate exact fallback

& [ECSProjectionAlternative] is considered but not selected
  + semantic subjects may project to runtime entity handles
  + typed immutable facets may project to components
  + compiler passes, faculties, planners, validators, rear reviewers, and effect gates may project to systems
  + system schedules may derive from Planner dependency and access graphs
  + command buffers may carry proposed changes until Observer or EffectBroker admission
  + every handle, component, query, system, and command maps back to canonical identities and versions
  + contextual n-ary relations remain explicit graph records when component attachment would lose meaning
  + component presence never proves truth, authority, admissibility, or execution role
  + selection requires measured semantic correspondence, replay, performance, and proof overhead against a graph-only fallback

& [PhysicalDesignDeferral] is binding
  + file repository, relational database, graph database, event store, object store, vector index, ECS, in-memory DAG, or hybrid layout remain candidates
  + sequential, actor, thread, process, service, multi-machine, or model-mediated lanes remain candidates
  + Rust types, SQL schema, ECS framework, serialization format, clock library, solver, provider, Git adapter, and calendar adapter remain unselected
  + physical indexes and caches cannot become semantic truth

